# Pocket Goblin visual identity

Canonical reference (full sheets only — never crop for production):

`docs/assets/pocket-goblin-fantasy-asset-library.jpg`

## Character lock

The Pocket Goblin is a small, friendly woodland helper:

- Bright green skin, large expressive eyes, very large pointed ears
- Brown leather aviator goggles with brass rims on the forehead
- Brown leather vest/tunic, backpack, sturdy boots
- Warm, painterly storybook look — cozy and helpful, never aggressive

Do **not** recreate the character with emoji, CSS shapes, Lucide/generic icons as a stand-in mascot, or generic AI-generated goblins. Prefer existing in-repo imagery until dedicated cut assets ship.

## Palette (woodland fantasy)

Prefer these directions when adjusting UI tokens or new surfaces:

| Role | Hex | Notes |
|------|-----|--------|
| Forest green | `#4A5D23` | Primary brand / foliage |
| Leather brown | `#8B5A2B` | Character gear, borders |
| Parchment | `#F5E6BE` | Soft backgrounds, cards |
| Warm oak | `#D4A373` | Accents, banners |

Avoid purple-on-white, cold neon, or flat SaaS greys that fight the den aesthetic.

## Asset usage

- Do **not** crop individual characters/icons from the reference sheets for production UI.
- Dedicated export assets will replace current placeholder imagery later.
- Until then: preserve current layout/functionality; when touching visuals, align colours/tone toward the palette above without inventing a new goblin.

## UI tone

- Rounded containers, parchment-like calm surfaces, readable text (low cognitive load).
- Capacity modes: Goblin (leaf / low energy), Steady (sun / balanced), Quest (mountains / high energy) — woodland metaphors, not corporate badges.
- Empty states and feedback should feel storybook and non-punitive when real assets arrive.
